cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Channels with memory: certified capacity windows for the dicode erasure and (1,inf)-RLL erasure and flip channels"
authors:
  - name: "Moki & Julio"
version: "1.0"
license: [CC-BY-4.0, MIT]
keywords:
  - channel capacity
  - channels with memory
  - dicode erasure channel
  - run-length limited constraint
  - certified computation
  - duality upper bound
  - ball arithmetic
abstract: >-
  Certified (rigorous) floors and ceilings on the capacity without feedback of three binary channels whose output depends
  on the previous input - the dicode erasure channel, the (1,inf)-RLL input-constrained binary erasure channel and the
  (1,inf)-RLL input-constrained binary symmetric channel - at five noise levels each. Ceilings are order-k dual bounds
  checked in exact rational arithmetic with upward-rounded logarithms; floors are Birch-type lower bounds on the information rates of explicit
  Markov inputs with a written rounding-error bound. Widths range from 8.1e-13 to 1.2e-4 bits per use; every window is
  consistent with the published proven ranges we compared with; at dicode erasure rate 0.1 our ceiling is below the best published analytic
  ceiling (and the published floor there is higher than ours). An independent second implementation agrees at the three standard points. Sealed (pre-registered) tests with
  their failures, referee reports, certificates and transcripts are included. Code is MIT-licensed (LICENSE-CODE).
  Written with AI assistance.
